<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Mansa State</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Mansa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Chavda Rajput state in northern Gujarat whose rulers claimed descent from the founders of medieval Anhilwad Patan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mansa">Mansa</a> was held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chavda-dynasty">Chavda</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajputs</a>, who traced their line to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chavda-dynasty">Chavda dynasty</a> that founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patan-gujarat">Anhilwad Patan</a> in the 8th century. The family established its holding around Mansa by about 1600.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The ruler governed a small agricultural territory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahi-kantha-agency">Mahi Kantha</a> region, paying tribute through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaekwads">Gaekwads of Baroda</a> and supervised by the British Mahi Kantha Agency. Few further details of its rulers are widely recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mansa">Mansa</a> merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bombay-presidency">Bombay Province</a> in 1948 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in 1960. The town now lies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gandhinagar">Gandhinagar</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mansa-state.jpg" alt="Mansa State" width="200" height="123"><figcaption>Image: Xufanc · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Mansa.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mansa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mansa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=mansa-state" aria-label="Mansa State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6639 1082 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mansa State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6959 1338L7364 1601M6959 1338L7364 1602M6959 1338L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6959 1338h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6959 1338h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mansa. <a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=mansa-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
